---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
    title="SF Ruby News - July 2026"
    description="July 2026 edition of SF Ruby News: Anthropic picks Persona to verify Claude users. Instacart becomes Gemini's first grocery partner. Gusto crosses $1B in revenue. RubyLLM hits the Hacker News front page. RubyConf 2026 in Las Vegas with Matz and Ruby Runway. SF Ruby Conf CFP opens July 6, early bird tickets July 15."
>
    <section class="relative px-night text-white overflow-hidden min-h-screen">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative z-10 pt-32 pb-16">

            <!-- Issue Navigation -->
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-8 text-sm">
                <a href="/news/2026-06/" class="text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors flex items-center gap-1">
                    <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" /></svg>
                    June 2026
                </a>
                <span class="text-white/30">Latest issue</span>
            </div>

            <!-- Masthead -->
            <div class="border-2 border-white/30 bg-white/5 px-4 py-3 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-12">
                <a href="/#news" class="px-font text-sm md:text-base text-white hover:text-gold-400 transition-colors">SF Ruby News</a>
                <p class="px-font text-px10 md:text-xs text-gold-400">World 07-26 &#8226; July</p>
            </div>

            <!-- News Carousel -->
            <div class="relative" id="news-carousel">

                <!-- Page 1 -->
                <div class="news-page" data-page="0">
                    <!-- Headline Story: Anthropic picks Persona -->
                    <div class="px-dialog p-6 md:p-8 mb-10">
                        <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-ruby-500 text-white text-px8 border-2 border-ink mb-4">Press</span>
                        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold text-white mb-6 leading-tight">Anthropic Picks Persona to Verify Claude Users</h2>
                        <div class="border-l-4 border-ruby-500 pl-6">
                            <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-white/80 leading-relaxed">
                                Starting July 8, <strong class="text-white">Anthropic</strong> will verify the identity of flagged <strong class="text-white">Claude</strong> accounts with a government ID and a selfie check, and it chose <strong class="text-white">Persona</strong>, the SF identity platform that calls itself a Rails-first company, to run the verification.
                            </p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mt-4">
                                TechCrunch, Gizmodo, and PYMNTS all covered the rollout, which applies to a flagged subset of Free, Pro, and Max accounts. For Persona ($418M raised, $2B valuation), it lands a month after FedRAMP Moderate authorization: one of the most closely watched AI labs now runs its trust layer on a Ruby company.
                            </p>
                            <div class="mt-4">
                                <p class="text-xs text-white/50">June 22, 2026 · TechCrunch</p>
                            </div>
                            <a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/06/22/anthropic-says-claude-may-want-to-see-your-id/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 mt-3 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                Read the coverage<span class="sr-only"> about Anthropic choosing Persona for Claude identity verification</span>
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 6H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2v-4M14 4h6m0 0v6m0-6L10 14" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Divider -->
                    <div class="h-[2px] bg-white/15 mb-10"></div>

                    <!-- Three Column Stories: Row 1 (events) -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-5 mb-10">
                        <!-- Conference: SF Ruby Startup Conference -->
                        <div class="px-dialog p-5 md:p-6">
                            <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-ruby-500 text-white text-px8 border-2 border-ink mb-3">Conference</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">SF Ruby Conf: CFP July 6, Tickets July 15</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">November 10–12, 2026 · SFJAZZ</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">Our first conference: three days at <strong class="text-white/80">SFJAZZ</strong> in San Francisco, keynoted by <strong class="text-white/80">Garry Tan</strong>, President &amp; CEO of Y Combinator. The CFP opens July 6, early bird tickets go on sale for one day on July 15, and sponsorships are open now.</p>
                            <a href="/conference-2026" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                Conference details<span class="sr-only"> for the SF Ruby Startup Conference</span>
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Event: RubyConf 2026 Las Vegas -->
                        <div class="px-dialog p-5 md:p-6">
                            <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-ruby-500 text-white text-px8 border-2 border-ink mb-3">Event</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">RubyConf 2026: Matz Keynotes Vegas</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">July 14–16, 2026 · Red Rock Resort</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">Ruby Central's flagship lands in Las Vegas with keynotes from <strong class="text-white/80">Matz</strong>, Dave Thomas, Jessica Kerr, and Obie Fernandez, plus the first class of Ruby Fellows. SF meetup regulars fill the program: Cameron Dutro, Jeremy Evans, Alexander Baygeldin, Marco Roth.</p>
                            <a href="https://rubyconf.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                Register<span class="sr-only"> for RubyConf 2026 Las Vegas</span>
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Event: SF Ruby Meetup July -->
                        <div class="px-dialog p-5 md:p-6">
                            <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-ruby-500 text-white text-px8 border-2 border-ink mb-3">Event</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">SF Ruby Meetup, July @ Sentry</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">July 22, 2026 · 45 Fremont St.</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">A new format: fewer talks, more connecting, with a full round of stage intros. Cameron Dutro presents Garnet.js, his JavaScript implementation of the YARV virtual machine, joined by Alexander Baygeldin (Evil Martians) and Marco Roth, all three fresh off the RubyConf stage the week before. 83+ RSVPs already.</p>
                            <a href="https://lu.ma/qeg0w8on" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                RSVP on Luma<span class="sr-only"> - SF Ruby July meetup at Sentry</span>
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Three Column Stories: Row 2 (business) -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-5 mb-6">
                        <div class="px-dialog p-5 md:p-6">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-gold-500 text-ink text-px8 border-2 border-ink w-fit">Release</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Instacart Is Gemini's First Grocery Partner</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">Gemini users can now connect <strong class="text-white/80">Instacart</strong> and build a real, shoppable cart in conversation, then check out for delivery or pickup (May 19). Gemini joins Claude and ChatGPT among the major assistants with agentic Instacart shopping. In June the Rails-built platform shipped Immersive Feed, a shoppable video ad format launching with brands like Siete Foods and Hellmann's.</p>
                                <a href="https://company.instacart.com/updates/instacart-brings-agentic-grocery-shopping-to-gemini" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-gold-400 hover:text-gold-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read more<span class="sr-only"> about Instacart's Gemini integration</span>
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="px-dialog p-5 md:p-6">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-gold-500 text-ink text-px8 border-2 border-ink w-fit">Release</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Chime Pushes Into Investing</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">CEO Chris Britt says investment accounts arrive within months: individual stocks, ETFs, bonds, and robo-investing powered by <strong class="text-white/80">Jade</strong>, Chime's generative-AI agent (June 1). The Rails-built neobank, 10.2M active members strong, keeps widening its lane after posting its first GAAP-profitable quarter this spring.</p>
                                <a href="https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/article/chime-ceo-says-hundreds-of-thousands-of-its-members-are-setting-up-trump-accounts-as-it-pushes-into-investing-161148607.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-gold-400 hover:text-gold-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read more<span class="sr-only"> about Chime's investing products</span>
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="px-dialog p-5 md:p-6">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-emerald-600 text-white text-px8 border-2 border-ink w-fit">Press</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Gusto Crosses $1B in Revenue</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">A milestone we missed last month: the Rails-built payroll and HR platform passed <strong class="text-white/80">$1 billion</strong> in trailing twelve-month recognized revenue (May 7) and has been cash-flow positive for several years. Fortune and TechCrunch both read the announcement, at a $9.3B valuation, as a step toward public markets.</p>
                                <a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/07/gusto-hits-1b-revenue-a-figure-that-brings-it-closer-to-public-markets/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read more<span class="sr-only"> about Gusto's $1B revenue milestone</span>
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Hiring strip -->
                    <div class="mt-4 mb-6 border-2 border-gold-500/50 px-6 py-4 flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center gap-3 md:gap-6">
                        <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-gold-500 text-ink text-px8 border-2 border-ink w-fit shrink-0">Hiring</span>
                        <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed flex-1">Ruby roles on the board: <strong class="text-white/80">Gusto</strong> (Staff, Payments/Risk), <strong class="text-white/80">Superconductor</strong> (Principal Rails), <strong class="text-white/80">Koah Labs</strong>, <strong class="text-white/80">Omada Health</strong>, <strong class="text-white/80">CompanyCam</strong>, plus Thatch, Persona, Chime, Patch, Reset, and Finta. New Rails teams hiring this month: <strong class="text-white/80">Y Combinator</strong> (Product Eng, SF), <strong class="text-white/80">WindBorne</strong> (Redwood City), <strong class="text-white/80">Opendate</strong>, and <strong class="text-white/80">Jukebox Health</strong>.</p>
                        <a href="/jobs" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-gold-400 hover:text-gold-300 transition-colors shrink-0">
                            Browse all jobs<span class="sr-only"> on the SF Ruby jobs board</span>
                            <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                        </a>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Page 2 -->
                <div class="news-page hidden" data-page="1">
                    <!-- Headline Story: RubyLLM on HN -->
                    <div class="px-dialog p-6 md:p-8 mb-10">
                        <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-ruby-500 text-white text-px8 border-2 border-ink mb-4">AI + Ruby</span>
                        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold text-white mb-6 leading-tight">RubyLLM Hits the Hacker News Front Page</h2>
                        <div class="border-l-4 border-ruby-500 pl-6">
                            <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-white/80 leading-relaxed">
                                <strong class="text-white">RubyLLM</strong> spent June 24 on the Hacker News front page with 446 points and 82 comments, the loudest mainstream moment yet for <strong class="text-white">Carmine Paolino's</strong> library.
                            </p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mt-4">
                                The timing was earned: v1.16 shipped days earlier with concurrent AI tool execution in threads or fibers, observability instrumentation without monkey patching, and proxy support for every provider. At 4,200+ GitHub stars and climbing 250 a month, RubyLLM is maturing from a beloved API wrapper into production agent infrastructure.
                            </p>
                            <div class="mt-4">
                                <p class="text-xs text-white/50">June 24, 2026 · Hacker News</p>
                            </div>
                            <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48660711" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 mt-3 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                Read the thread<span class="sr-only"> - RubyLLM on Hacker News</span>
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 6H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2v-4M14 4h6m0 0v6m0-6L10 14" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Divider -->
                    <div class="h-[2px] bg-white/15 mb-10"></div>

                    <!-- Three Column Stories: Row 1 (community) -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-5 mb-10">
                        <!-- Event: Brighton Ruby recap -->
                        <div class="px-dialog p-5 md:p-6">
                            <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-ruby-500 text-white text-px8 border-2 border-ink mb-3">Event</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Brighton Ruby Runs Its 12th Edition</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">June 25, 2026 · Brighton Dome</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">Andy Croll's single-day seaside conference delivered 11 talks: Iliana Hadzhiatanasova on 15 years of upgrades in a 3-million-line monolith (Rails 3.0 to edge), Craig Norford on scaling multi-tenant Sidekiq, a performance-engineering session from Elena Tănăsoiu and Emma Gabriel, and Brian Casel on why your experience is your AI advantage.</p>
                            <a href="https://rubyevents.org/events/brightonruby-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                See the program<span class="sr-only"> - Brighton Ruby 2026</span>
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Event: June meetup recap -->
                        <div class="px-dialog p-5 md:p-6">
                            <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-ruby-500 text-white text-px8 border-2 border-ink mb-3">Event</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">SF Ruby Meetup @ PlanetScale</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">June 18, 2026 · San Francisco</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">Hosted with Sam Lambert. Jeremy Evans (Ubicloud) walked through implementing Core Set, Hal Spitz delivered "ActiveJob: Call Me Maybe," and Irina Nazarova demoed local-first Rails with pglite and Electric, plus making Ruby resources discoverable to LLMs.</p>
                            <a href="https://lu.ma/ltipgvuh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                Event page<span class="sr-only"> - SF Ruby June meetup at PlanetScale</span>
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Event: Blastoff Rails recordings -->
                        <div class="px-dialog p-5 md:p-6">
                            <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-ruby-500 text-white text-px8 border-2 border-ink mb-3">Event</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Blastoff Rails Recordings Are Live</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">June 11–12, 2026 · Albuquerque</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">All 17 talks from the first-edition conference are up on rubyevents.org, including keynotes from Irina Nazarova ("Startups on Rails") and Kieran Klaassen ("Building Cora Solo"), plus Avi Flombaum's "Don't Read the Code: Trusting AI With Your Rails Codebase."</p>
                            <a href="https://rubyevents.org/events/blastoffrails-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                Watch the talks<span class="sr-only"> - Blastoff Rails 2026 recordings</span>
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Three Column Stories: Row 2 -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-5 mb-6">
                        <div class="px-dialog p-5 md:p-6">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-emerald-600 text-white text-px8 border-2 border-ink w-fit">Press</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Rails at 41 Million Requests an Hour</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">Andrew Atkinson documents how <strong class="text-white/80">Aura Frames</strong> survived Christmas Day: 41M API requests an hour and 226K database transactions a second across eight sharded Postgres primaries, on Rails' built-in Multiple Databases support with disable_joins, keyset pagination, and Memcached (June 16). A scaling proof point to bookmark.</p>
                                <a href="https://andyatkinson.com/how-aura-frames-scales-for-peak-load-ruby-on-rails" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read the case study<span class="sr-only"> about Aura Frames scaling Rails</span>
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="px-dialog p-5 md:p-6">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-ruby-500 text-white text-px8 border-2 border-ink w-fit">AI + Ruby</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Matz's AI-Built Compiler Runs Rails in 13MB of RAM</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">Sam Ruby compiled a Rails blog app through Roundhouse into <strong class="text-white/80">Spinel</strong>, the ahead-of-time Ruby compiler Matz is building with Claude's help, producing a native binary that runs in 13MB of RAM (June 19). Spinel covers a deliberate Ruby subset, and it points at Ruby on the edge and in embedded devices.</p>
                                <a href="https://intertwingly.net/blog/2026/06/19/Spinel-on-Rails.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read the writeup<span class="sr-only"> about Spinel on Rails</span>
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="px-dialog p-5 md:p-6">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-gold-500 text-ink text-px8 border-2 border-ink w-fit">Hiring</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Y Combinator Builds on Rails (and Is Hiring)</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">YC's software team, about 20 engineers behind Work at a Startup, Demo Day, GStack, and GBrain, is hiring Product Engineers in SF on a stack of Rails, React, Postgres, and LLM APIs. The accelerator whose president keynotes our conference in November ships on Ruby.</p>
                                <a href="https://www.ycombinator.com/software" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-gold-400 hover:text-gold-300 transition-colors">
                                    See the roles<span class="sr-only"> on Y Combinator's software team</span>
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Three Column Stories: Row 3 -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-5 mb-6">
                        <div class="px-dialog p-5 md:p-6">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-gold-500 text-ink text-px8 border-2 border-ink w-fit">Release</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Chatwoot Tops Ruby Trending, Ships Voice Calls</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">The Rails-built open-source support platform (YC W21) added 4,100+ GitHub stars this month, the most of any Ruby repo, and launched voice calls in beta: Twilio phone calls and WhatsApp calling alongside Captain, its AI support agent (June 16).</p>
